course: dictionary
lesson: 4398
title: Hairstyles in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hairstyle is the way someone's hair is cut and arranged. A ponytail, a plait and a bob are all hairstyles. If you do not know a word, look at the words around it, because they are its context and often give you clues.
explain: Read this: «The Terracotta Army near Xi'an was found in 1974 by farmers digging a well; its thousands of life-size clay soldiers have different faces and hairstyles.» The words «different faces» tell you the soldiers do not all look the same, so «hairstyles» must show a difference too, in the way their hair is done.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try "different faces and the way their hair is cut and arranged". It still makes sense, so you have understood the word correctly.
fact: A hairstyle is the way someone's hair is cut and arranged.
fact: «A new hairstyle» means a different way of cutting or arranging your hair.
fact: In stories, a hairstyle can help you picture a character.
fact: The Terracotta Army was found in 1974 by farmers digging a well near Xi'an.
fact: Its clay soldiers were made from shared moulds, with details added by hand, so their hairstyles and faces can differ.
exercise: What is a hairstyle? | The colour of someone's eyes | *The way someone's hair is cut and arranged | The clothes a person wears | A hat worn in winter
exercise: In «The soldiers have different faces and hairstyles», what does hairstyles mean? | The places where they stood | *The ways their hair is cut and arranged | Their shoes | Their weapons
exercise: Which of these is a hairstyle? | A bus ticket | A pencil case | A football | *A ponytail
test: Which word means the way hair is cut and arranged? | Shoelace | Hairbrush | *Hairstyle | Hatband
test: The clay soldiers have different faces and hairstyles. What does this tell you? | The soldiers were made from one mould with no changes | *Each soldier's hair is cut and arranged in its own way | All the soldiers look exactly the same | The soldiers were all carved from one block of wood
exam: Which sentence uses hairstyle correctly? | Maya's hairstyle is the colour of the sky | The hairstyle was a loud noise in the kitchen | *Maya changed her hairstyle and now wears a plait | Maya drank a glass of hairstyle at lunch
